WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.430
You've already talked with the others right?

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.320
You know what it means to have
crossed the Golden Bridge, don't you?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.150
Young Master,

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.620
thank you.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.550
And sorry.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:45.020
Kai-chan, just like you said, he's not loyal at all.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:52.390
Let us paint the sky with a rainbow of colors

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:22.520
We drew a scribbled map of the future with no defined end

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.220
But you smiled saying, "no matter how lost we get,

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.740
or how much we cry, the end will come"

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:39.900
If tomorrow was an untouched white canvas

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.610
I'd like to see what kind of colors would shine the brightest

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.960
Like tears leaving behind a rainbow

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.900
I'll prove to you I can change this world

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.230
Let us paint the sky with a rainbow of colors

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.270
Listening to the footsteps of a tomorrow

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:07.450
whose name we've yet to know

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.750
Before they knew it, half a month had passed.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.160
Following the steps of Kaiunho and Ochu,

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.640
many had successfully activated missions.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.540
But only a few managed to clear
them and move on from the village.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.090
Get out of my house, you cheater!

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.920
Ho-chan, please let me explain,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.010
please, Ho-chan!

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.390
I thought it might have been
some rare item, but it's just you.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.890
Oriku.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.270
Seems like things didn't go well with that lady.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.990
Well well, my deepest condolences.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:59.420
Please don't let me get in your way,
see you later host-chan.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.800
Wait,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:06.020
I know your servant and that fatty only managed
to clear the missions because of you, right?

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:12.420
As you can see I've been trying really
hard as a host, and I was almost there!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.920
I've already abandoned
my pride, please help us too!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.650
What I have for you is one piece of advice.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:26.930
Even if it's going well now,
it won't last for more than 10 years.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.640
I've got no time for small fry like you.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.810
My perfect plan to clear
a mission is already in motion.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.570
Now, let's earn some test points.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:38.190
Challenge Upon Challenge

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.280
Hey, Isn't that Oriku?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.240
Why is he doing that?

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.910
So Oriku's finally back in action,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.870
this is gonna to get interesting.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.870
Oh my, thank you very much.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.630
Why is he helping Aunt Ko carry water?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:02.900
According to our info, Aunt Ko is just a normal
villager without any special missions right?

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.890
Then there's nothing to gain by helping her.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.120
He must know something we don't.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.610
You must be tired, please
have some food before going.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.730
Thanks.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.980
Oh, that's right, would you mind taking
this to my son's school for me?

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.550
School?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.900
What is this?

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.990
I brought you something from Aunt Ko.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.730
Thank you very much.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.580
Hey, who said you could
write in my book like that!?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.090
You were stuck on the last
word of that poem, right?

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.610
This is marvelous!

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.590
This is exactly what I needed! Thank you.
Is there anything I can do for you?

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:51.270
I don't need anything special, but could
I have that towel you always use?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.180
My towel?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.690
What is he gonna do with that stinky towel?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.740
Doesn't he smell anything?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.690
You're really something else, Oriku.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.070
Huh? Isn't that Ho-chan's house?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.020
What do you want?

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.360
This smell! It's definitely that person's smell!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.880
Oh that's right...Ho-chan has
feelings for that teacher.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.040
This is my hand made steamed meat.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:33.190
Just like that, Oriku continued to trade items
to get everyone what they wanted.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:37.350
In this way, he managed to gain the favor
of all 120 villagers in a single day.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.520
Thus, bringing to completion
his Stinky Towel Protocol.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.740
Is there any point to the things that Oriku is doing?

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.810
After being here for almost a month,
everyone should already be clear on the fact that...

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:52.030
Being on good terms with the villagers is nothing but a switch to activate a certain mission.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.370
And there's only one mission per villager.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.500
In other words, if that person's
mission is already cleared,

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.860
there's no point in trying to be
on good terms with them anymore.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.200
Then why?

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:10.070
Indeed, of all the 120 villagers, there's almost no one that still has a mission to offer.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.470
Except one extra person.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:17.660
I didn't think you guys were this stupid.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.980
You really think that those 120
people are <i>all</i> the villagers?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.080
What, there's no one else right?

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.810
If we count the unborn baby
inside Aunt Cho's womb..

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.240
Or is it that dogs and pigs also have missions?

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.450
You guys, your stupidity
really knows no bounds.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:33.580
What did you say!?

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.790
I don't know what you're trying to do, but ...

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:35.790
It pisses me off!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.120
Is it because you're inbreeds?

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.620
Get him!

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.330
The 121st villager, it's been a while.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.180
Can you tell me what you want?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.180
Seeing how smart I am, even if your mission is world peace I just might be able to achieve it.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.600
Not yet enough.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:03.150
Not enough? I see.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:09.110
Oriku believed that "not enough" was referring to the closeness of his relationships with the villagers.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.890
Activating the hidden mission
is supposed be no small feat.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:19.250
However, Oriku was able to fully satisfy
each villager's need, with great efficiency.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.130
Oriku is doing some pretty impressive stuff,
but isn't he going overboard?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.110
Also, satisfying the villagers doesn't seem to be...

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:31.970
Connected to clearing the mission
for the guy in the black suit.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.060
Oriku!? He came to pick a fight again?

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.930
He must have heard us talking about him!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.270
He's been stalking us!

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.140
Idiots, you're the children of dogs!

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:46.020
Calm down, he's baiting us into fighting.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.030
You scared? Where's the big talk
about your prestigious families?

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.030
Say that again!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:56.030
Your mothers had sex with dogs
and conceived you guys right?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.280
How insolent!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.160
Or are you guys born out
of the Ryoi club sticking inside..

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.670
Look here, you! Stop intentionally trying to pick fights!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.840
I'm not your personal bodyguard!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.340
I should almost be there, I think.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:17.600
Almost everyone's satisfaction levels are maxed,

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.510
except for...

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.160
Fine, my mission is simple. Give me money.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.670
One coin would be enough.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.450
Money?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:31.360
Wait, not normal money. It has to be the money used on this mountain.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.570
You mean the Reiken Mountain?

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.820
You should already have it.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.410
Inside Togen village, there's no such thing as money.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:47.340
Everything is bartered,
so it can't be from this village.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.880
But the Reikei town at the foot of the mountain...

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.010
This money from the Reikei Town
should be from the mountain.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.640
If you don't want it,
you can always throw it away.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.890
<i>This coin was a reward for helping
the innkeeper win the bet.</i>

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.930
Yeah, that will work.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.150
Sorry, I changed my mind.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.280
This coin is a memento from my dead wife,
I can't just give it away!

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:18.200
Who's your dead wife again?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.700
Money? What is that?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:26.800
A currency, for trading things of the same value.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.320
Currency? Trade?

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:33.930
Oh, I get what you mean,

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.970
but there's only a few people in this village.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.840
We're satisfied with just bartering.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.350
Like I said, we can start using it.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:46.730
This will make trading more efficient,
leading to an increase in productivity.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.170
You can also trade with the outside world,

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.980
which will make the village grow,
which will lead to everyone living a better life.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:57.030
And all I ask for my reward is one coin.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:58.810
No way.

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:03.870
Why!? Aren't we already best friends?
Why don't you trust me, please tell me the reason.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:12.000
I know it's for the village, but I can't just change our villages traditions that were set generations ago.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.900
What you said is wonderful,

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.340
but unfortunately it's not something I'd prefer.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:21.650
Mayor, you're far too old
to be trying to act all cute.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.600
Be careful or you might
one day die of a heart attack.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.120
Obu, isn't this enough?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:33.880
This kid likes to play tricks. He should be
grateful that I let him continue in the contest.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:38.570
Just because he found a glitch in your design?

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.630
You don't understand anything at all.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:44.080
That's not a glitch,

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.250
my designs are always perfect.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.500
Seriously, where do you get that confidence from?

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:57.340
Anyway, why do you take his side?
What about our long lasting friendship?

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:01.220
Well, all thanks to him,
I don't have to go back home.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.900
I can't help but want to help him.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:08.100
Anyway, shouldn't you behave more like an elder of the Heavenly Sword Hall?

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:15.860
Behave like an Elder? Don't be ridiculous! It's not like there's a pay-bonus for me even if I do behave.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:21.150
Jeez, I hope they give me a bonus,

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.460
if I don't get it, who knows what I'll do...

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:28.650
I'd like to see what you'd do, Obu.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.000
You want to quit being an elder?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.580
Chief! Welcome...

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.590
Quit it, this is my house!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:40.170
Is that so? I thought I was at home.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:43.060
Recently, I've been feeling kind of lost...

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:47.060
But I'm too poor to fix it, could you help?

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:50.340
How about you fix that shameless
attitude of yours first?

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:55.110
Changing the designs without my consent, maybe you should forget about your salary for this year.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.330
If you keep going on like this,
you can quit being an elder.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.740
Go back to your Amorphic Peak
and re-cultivate yourself.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:05.990
Maybe I'll reconsider giving you the position of Elder after you've reached the stage of Nascent Soul.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:12.500
Everything I've done is in the interest of the sect. If you don't understand that, you're gonna regret it.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.670
You stingy myopic old geezer.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:24.680
Guess I should fix it if there really is a glitch.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:28.810
I feel like I've seen that
boy somewhere else before.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.310
Oh well nevermind, can't see
clearly without my glasses anyway.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:41.070
Damn it, Oriku that bastard.
Why can't he just leave us alone?

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.570
Maybe he's just frustrated.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.700
Wouldn't it be fun to see his face
when he can't finish the mission.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.080
Hey dogs!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.040
Again!?

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.880
Didn't I just tell you to stop picking fights!?

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.110
This is the last time, I promise.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.460
You've already given up?

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.550
There's no such thing as money in this village,

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:07.530
but if you're asking for money, that means you know how it works.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.390
Which means, you yourself might have some.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.100
If so, could you give me some?

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.820
So you're gonna take money
from me, and then return it.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:26.130
That's a nice idea, and not against the
rules, but I can't just hand it to you.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:33.270
And I won't trade you with gold or silver,
as they hold no worth on the mountain.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:38.330
Or are you going to take it by force?
No matter what you choose, I'm ready for it.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:43.550
I already know that things from
the outside don't hold any value,

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.840
which is why I'm gonna trade you
with things from the mountain.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.650
Hey, are you sure?

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:52.170
It's clearly a key that's supposed
to be used somewhere else.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.100
You're gonna use it it in this small village?

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:58.100
With a rarity rating of zero,
and an obvious "Backdoor" written on it,

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:03.630
compared to the coin that the Game Master
tried so hard to get from me...

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:06.450
The choice is obvious.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.360
You're definitely an interesting fellow,

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.520
All right I'll take the key.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:17.540
It is indeed something from this mountain, and it is valuable to me.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.670
Congratulations. You've completed the mission.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.430
Now that I'm finally on my own,

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.520
I'm not gonna waste this chance!

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:40.770
The three idiots you tried to pick fights with
also cleared their missions accidentally,

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.020
so they'll follow after you.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.430
Please go this way, good luck.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:58.080
So this crafty kid also cleared it.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:02.480
What is that key for, Rei-chan?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.590
The key to the safe that holds
the money from selling the radishes.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:11.890
What? You used such an important
thing as an item in the contest, why!?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:17.560
I just thought it would be fun,
having something like a bet.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.320
What an expensive bet!

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.860
What if he failed, despite your wishes?

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.280
But he cleared it, right?

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:31.490
I think he already has an idea
as to who is inside this black suit.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.370
Rei-chan, are you a pedophile?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.020
Die, you 200 year old hag.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:36.830
How mean.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:11.530
The reward is automatically decided based
on the points you earned in Togen village.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:19.880
Which means that these kids will at least
have a chance to make it to the goal.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:24.920
Though it's been tens of years since
anyone has actually made it.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:33.450
In other words, it's a design filled with kindness
that doesn't frustrate the newbies. Don't you agree?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.930
Whatever, even without making it to the end,
the best one can just join the sect anyway.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.340
You're so hard to please.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.350
You're one to talk.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:51.930
Don't you feel so fulfilled being a teacher?
Some of these kids have great potential.

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.490
It's all because of me that you get to see them,

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.740
how are you gonna thank me?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.580
Stop the chitchat, as the elder
of the Heavenly Sword Hall,

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.120
you're supposed to be supervising the contest.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:07.040
I just didn't want him to feel too lonely.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.570
You're the reason that our
gambling was found out.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:10.740
It's my fault?

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.630
Thanks to that, I'll have to stay here on duty.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:20.060
With the contest almost half way done,
you're saying that there are kids with great potential?

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:25.180
Having made it this far, they're all good kids.

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:28.300
However, things will get difficult at Icewind Valley.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:32.710
The first one to have cleared Togen village, Kaiunho,

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:37.990
although he has a mediocre score, as the first person
to clear, he should have gotten a good reward.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:45.960
Although he only has slightly above average potential, and a tier 3 Spirit Base, he looks really promising.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.560
It's been half a month since I left the village.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.090
I managed to avoid the traps
and monsters along the way,

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:55.260
and the reward I got was the Downgrade Doll.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:18:00.890
Having made it so far, I still can't
stop shaking from excitement.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:05.810
Now!

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:06.810
3 Tier Downgrade!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:22.200
It's still so powerful after losing 3 tiers.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.220
Kaiunho-sama!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:46.850
It's me, Ochu. It's been a while.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.100
Fancy meeting you here.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:54.780
Were you fighting by yourself?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:58.720
Yeah, I couldn't do a thing against it.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:06.310
I alone might not be of much help, but if we fight together, surely we can do something.

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:07.420
Right everyone?

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:13.460
After losing 3 tiers, it should be around level 2.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:17.920
If all six of us use our items well enough,
we should be able to defeat it.

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.430
Hold on, what's happening!?

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:30.560
Didn't it lose levels? It's getting bigger and bigger.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.060
The monster leveled up five times.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:38.070
What's going on? Is this the kindness
you were talking about?

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:46.950
Yes, against one opponent it's at Tier Level 3. So naturally, it should be stronger against six.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.330
The more opponents it faces,
the more powerful it becomes.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.460
It's a system that has taken into
account the number of players.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.000
Isn't that real kindness?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:57.960
How is that so?

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:03.340
It doesn't matter what you say now.
At this rate, no one's going to pass it.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.900
Well, these kids might not.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:09.310
Then what's the point, everyone will fail.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:14.480
<i>These</i> kids can't but that
doesn't mean everyone will fail.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:17.360
Here he comes!

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:23.700
Isn't that Oriku?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.450
Why is he there? Isn't he supposed
to be half a month behind?

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:34.010
What, only good for three uses?

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:37.630
It was so convenient
for covering such long distances.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.770
C-Cloud Stepping Shoes?

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:41.380
So that's how he caught up.

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:46.100
O-san left the village with you guys...

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.260
He must have gotten some crazy items.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.270
His shoes were glowing just now.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.640
That's it.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.900
Did you guys also get some special items?

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:55.400
No...

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:57.860
What the...?

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:03.560
We were directly teleported here.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:04.450
Why?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.280
Kind of like...It doesn't
make a difference anyway.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.910
Don't say its name!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:11.500
And? What's next?

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:19.170
I see, so you're the next obstacle to clear.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.190
Next?

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:25.930
So he traveled around on Cloud Stepping Shoes and defeated the other monsters already?

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.930
Let me use my last item.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.930
The Mystic Frost Sword? How did such a high level item become a reward?

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:36.110
No way!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:38.660
Wait, why are you surprised?

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:41.690
Aren't you the one that designed the system?

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:46.240
The reward is decided automatically, based on points.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:51.340
He must have earned an absurd amount of points.

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:54.390
But, without any training

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:58.710
there's no way he can control high caliber items like the Cloud Stepping Shoes or the Mystic Frost Sword.

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:00.910
How?

00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:23.750
The beat that quivers
within my worn down memory,

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:27.220
Drowns in my slumber,

00:22:27.390 --> 00:22:29.060
sinking below the surface

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:35.080
My eyes, as they
look up to a pouring sky

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:40.480
Reflect a heart locked
away by the moonlight

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:51.330
Only my most twisted pain
lies within this weaving infinity

00:22:51.560 --> 00:22:57.770
Bleeding away miserably
as our intertwined fingers untangle

00:22:58.110 --> 00:23:01.500
Clinging to your feelings,

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:04.700
oh so powerfully

00:23:05.090 --> 00:23:10.260
I'll show you I can go
beyond this rusted world

00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:15.850
The words that pierced
through this permanent illusion

00:23:16.110 --> 00:23:25.950
Resound through my out stretched fingers

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.570
"After an Eternity".

00:23:37.570 --> 00:23:39.350
Waiting for you at the Reiken Mountain.
